<clickhouse>
    <!--
        INTENDED topology, one ClickHouse node PER MACHINE.

        Selected by CH_MEMORY_CONFIG=memory.distributed.xml (set in .env.intended)
        and used by docker-stack.stores.yml.

        The other two files in this directory cap a node because it is SHARING a
        host, and neither cap is right here:

          * memory.xml (1.1 GB) assumed six ClickHouse servers on one machine,
            splitting roughly 4.2 GB between them. With one node per machine that
            is needlessly tight — the node would spill or fail large queries while
            most of its machine sat idle.
          * memory.local.xml (2.5 GB) is the single-node testing cap, sized to
            leave room for MongoDB, Keeper, the gold store and the whole pipeline
            on the SAME machine.

        Here a store machine runs one ClickHouse server plus at most one Keeper
        (~150 MB) and one MongoDB member (~200 MB) or one PostgreSQL node, so the
        server can be given the clear majority of the machine. 4 GB assumes a
        machine with 8 GB of RAM; raise it in proportion on larger machines, which
        is the whole reason this is a separate file rather than a hard-coded value.

        NOTE: only SERVER-level settings belong in this file. Per-query limits
        such as max_memory_usage are profile settings and live in users.xml;
        placing them here prevents the server from starting.
    -->
    <max_server_memory_usage>4000000000</max_server_memory_usage>

    <!-- Caches are per node, and this node no longer shares its page cache with
         five siblings, so it can afford a larger mark cache than memory.xml. -->
    <mark_cache_size>536870912</mark_cache_size>
    <uncompressed_cache_size>0</uncompressed_cache_size>
</clickhouse>
